    "growth_rate_source": "judgment: revenue path anchored to FY2026 guidance (+2.9%), then ~2.5-3% nominal (10-year revenue CAGR of 4.3% includes the pandemic surge; the 5-year is 0.9%)",
    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity CAGRs are meaningless. FY2020 equity was $669M after mark-to-market pension losses (US GAAP MTM accounting), so the 5-year equity CAGR reads 89%. EPS 5-year (33%) starts from the same depressed FY2020 base. Both diverge by more than 30% from revenue. Neither is used.",
    "notes": "Owner-FCF CAGRs are ABOVE reported FCF CAGRs (5-year +2.0% vs -1.1%). This is the opposite of the usual pattern: SBC fell from $1.57B in FY2022 to $73M in FY2025, so less of today's cash flow is being paid away in stock than at the peak. The 3-year declines run from the FY2022 pandemic peak and describe the cycle unwinding, not the trend."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Amazon exit completes, SMB/healthcare refills the network, and margins recover to the 14.5% mid-cycle level (not the 16% pandemic peak) as automation savings net of wage inflation land by FY2029.",
    "bull": "Healthcare, cold-chain and SMB mix compound, and most of the $3B Network of the Future saving survives the 2028 labour contract. Margin returns to ~16% by FY2030.",
    "bear": "Volume lost to Amazon's own network and tariffs is not replaced, labour costs absorb the savings, and margin stays at ~12.5%. Dividend coverage breaks."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Mid-cycle, transition-adjusted owner-FCF DCF. The base case does not extrapolate the FY2021-22 peak (16% EBITDA margin, $9-10B FCF) or the trough H1-2026 GAAP print. Margins recover only to the ten-year average plus a partial automation credit, and every scenario's terminal value is capped at 12-14x FCF. The pension deficit and NCI are deducted as debt-like claims after net debt.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Margin recovery is the whole case. Each 1pp of mature EBITDA margin is worth roughly $0.9B a year of FCF, about $13/share at a 13x exit.",
      "The 2028 Teamsters contract could absorb the Network of the Future savings.",
      "Volume loss to Amazon Logistics is secular, not cyclical.",
      "Dividend above FCF in FY2025 raises leverage and could force a cut, which is a sentiment risk not captured in IV.",
      "Pension deficit is sensitive to discount rates; it is deducted at the 2026-06-30 book value.",
      "FY2026 guidance figures (revenue ~$91.2B, operating profit ~$8.65B, FCF ~$5.5B) are taken from the qualitative analysis and were not re-verified against the Q2-2026 8-K."
    ]
  },
